------------------------------------------------------------------------

Steps for running BusTalk simulations. 

Ensure that the following variables are set as per the user's
local environment settings.

eg : setenv GLOBAL /h/arm/global 

eg : setenv LIB_VHDL /AVANT/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/vital/cb25os163/zero  

eg : setenv LIB_SYNOP /NIS/backup/ARMOURY/armdata/AVANT/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/synopsys/cb25os163/1997.01/models

Please note that the above paths are EXAMPLE paths.

Additionally set the following environment variables to control
simulation. 

setenv PERIPH Aaci
setenv SIMULATOR modelsim
setenv TEST_METH scaninsert
setenv HDL_SOURCE vhdl
setenv HDL_NETL vhdl

1. VHDL RTL simulations
------------------------
- In the verification/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
  where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
  that needs to be used for simulations.

  [Please refer to verification/bustest/makefile for the 
   complete list of <testnames>.]

  This will create verification/bustest/invec/infile.bif

- In the verification/vhdl/ directory
  'make rtl'

2. VHDL SCAN NETLIST simulations
------------------------------------
- In the verification/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
  where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
  that needs to be used for simulations.

  [Please refer to verification/bustest/makefile for the 
   complete list of <testnames>.]

  This will create verification/bustest/invec/infile.bif

- In the verification/vhdl/ directory
  'make net_max'

  This will perform a MAXIMUM timing annotated simulation 
  on the scan-inserted VHDL netlist generated from VHDL
  RTL. 

